WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.280
28 Andean Rocks share a crystal signature that flags magma pulses before eruptions. This is Planetarian

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:12.900
Daily, episode 239. After the crystals come a muscle protein that blocks insulin, a histone

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.620
that cannot be swapped in sperm, and how tiny sequence changes lock proteins into irreplaceable

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:25.280
roles. University of Queensland researchers in a Fizz.org report examine thin cross sections

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.880
of volcanic rocks from seven volcanoes and two ancient super eruptions. The sample

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.580
spent 230 kilometers of the central Andes, and the work is published in Nature Communications.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:43.560
Ph.D. candidate Daniela Para and Calada measured chemistry in the smallest plagioclays microchrists,

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.300
crystals about as wide as a human hair, those newest crystals formed during the final stages of

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:54.940
eruption and lined up across samples of different ages and eruptive styles. The team named the

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.580
pattern the plagioclase eruptability field.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:03.240
Senior author Teresa Ubeid noted the pattern also appears in other pacific ring of fire

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:03.780
datasets.

00:01:04.906 --> 00:01:09.866
Scientists and findings carried by science daily found that accumulation of the protein

00:01:09.866 --> 00:01:13.126
Miro1 impairs insulin signaling in muscle tissue.

00:01:13.726 --> 00:01:18.666
Preclinical removal of Miro1 restored insulin responsiveness in the affected muscles.

00:01:19.346 --> 00:01:22.466
Exercise lowered Miro1 levels in people with diabetes.

00:01:22.466 --> 00:01:27.786
The work identifies a pathway contributing to insulin resistance that had not been recognized

00:01:27.786 --> 00:01:28.426
before.

00:01:29.335 --> 00:01:35.895
Kyushu University researchers in a Fizz.org report showed that the H3MM-15 sub variant

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:42.655
of histone H3.3 cannot be replaced by standard H3.3 during mouse spermatogenesis.

00:01:43.275 --> 00:01:46.695
The two proteins still produce distinct behavior inside chromatin.

00:01:48.075 --> 00:01:52.375
H3MM15 helps regulate gene expression required for normal sperm formation.

00:01:52.895 --> 00:01:57.575
Something most people get wrong about proteins is that a close sequence match can always take

00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:59.455
another place inside a living cell.

00:02:00.075 --> 00:02:05.055
A pair of histone proteins can differ at only three amino acids and still refuse to stand

00:02:05.055 --> 00:02:05.955
in for one another.

00:02:06.475 --> 00:02:10.775
That gap is small enough to look trivial on a sequence map and large enough to create

00:02:10.775 --> 00:02:13.015
functional roles that are not interchangeable.

00:02:13.015 --> 00:02:16.235
The cell is not averaging those three positions away.

00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:18.415
It is reading them as a different job.

00:02:19.055 --> 00:02:23.935
Miner sequence changes of that kind can lock a protein into a role no nearby variant can

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:26.715
fill, even when the rest of the chain looks the same.

00:02:27.295 --> 00:02:32.335
Today's other findings sit on the same scale, a small molecular or environmental detail

00:02:32.335 --> 00:02:36.095
that reshapes a much larger biological or geological process.

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.695
The point is not that every tiny difference matters equally.

00:02:39.695 --> 00:02:44.295
It is that a difference of three residues can be decisive when the job is specific.

00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:49.115
Substitution fails when chromatin needs one version and the standard version cannot

00:02:49.115 --> 00:02:50.295
supply that behavior.

00:02:50.935 --> 00:02:55.495
Sequence similarity is not the same thing as replaceability, and that is the assumption

00:02:55.495 --> 00:02:57.275
the three residue gap undercuts.

00:02:58.381 --> 00:03:03.221
University of Tokyo researchers applied a new radiocarbon method to a sediment core from

00:03:03.221 --> 00:03:07.981
the Kumano Sea in a study appearing in radiocarbon that Fizz.org covered.

00:03:07.981 --> 00:03:14.221
The analysis identified multiple hidden earthquake traces in the Nankai trough, reconstructing

00:03:14.221 --> 00:03:18.161
those events improves forecasts of future geophysical activity in the region.

00:03:19.052 --> 00:03:25.112
Researchers identified Lymo semion laranja, a tiny orange-patterned fish less than 3 cm

00:03:25.112 --> 00:03:27.292
long, in a science daily report.

00:03:27.912 --> 00:03:32.732
The species occurs only in three small forest pools threatened by mining, deforestation,

00:03:32.992 --> 00:03:33.492
and pollution.

00:03:33.492 --> 00:03:37.552
Its restricted range raises immediate conservation concerns.

00:03:37.712 --> 00:03:41.946
A team led by Siong Sikshin at Sungkyun Kwan University

00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:44.026
developed a liquid assisted growth method

00:03:44.026 --> 00:03:47.046
that produces perovskite semiconductor thin films

00:03:47.046 --> 00:03:50.486
with fewer defects in work Fizz.org reported.

00:03:50.886 --> 00:03:54.106
The same platform yielded both high-performance solar cells

00:03:54.106 --> 00:03:56.146
and light-emitting diodes or LEDs.

00:03:57.046 --> 00:04:00.106
International collaborators included institutions in Korea,

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.706
the United States, and Japan.

00:04:01.706 --> 00:04:07.093
Archaeologists examining social responses to extreme climate episodes in northern

00:04:07.093 --> 00:04:12.353
Peru's Lambayecque Valley found that violence remained extremely rare across the surveyed

00:04:12.353 --> 00:04:12.813
periods.

00:04:13.373 --> 00:04:18.313
Resource stress from catastrophic flooding was part of those El Nino events, yet conflict

00:04:18.313 --> 00:04:19.153
stayed scarce.

00:04:19.713 --> 00:04:24.793
The results challenge assumptions that ecological upheaval necessarily increases conflict or

00:04:24.793 --> 00:04:25.773
ritual sacrifice.

00:04:26.822 --> 00:04:31.842
Researchers developed a clinical simulation approach that incorporates care ethics, relational

00:04:31.842 --> 00:04:36.042
presence with patients and emotional management alongside technical skills.

00:04:36.622 --> 00:04:41.322
Earlier methods focused mainly on compliance and procedural standards from an interprofessional

00:04:41.322 --> 00:04:41.822
viewpoint.

00:04:42.502 --> 00:04:46.762
The new model addresses aspects of nursing practice previously overlooked in standard

00:04:46.762 --> 00:04:47.302
assessments.

00:04:48.369 --> 00:04:53.689
Columbia University and Universidad Adolfo Ibania's researchers describe structures within

00:04:53.689 --> 00:04:59.109
gravitational fields that can break and reconnect in an analysis science daily carried.

00:04:59.109 --> 00:05:01.689
The process transfers energy into matter.

00:05:02.029 --> 00:05:06.249
The finding emerges directly from analysis of the existing Einstein equations.

00:05:07.324 --> 00:05:14.264
Liang Bua Cave on Flores, in a Fizz.org report, yielded a leg bone dated between 190,000 and

00:05:14.264 --> 00:05:18.864
120,000 years old, that had been initially set aside as unremarkable.

00:05:19.484 --> 00:05:23.484
Reexamination established it as the largest known member of its bird group.

00:05:24.004 --> 00:05:27.944
The find comes from the same cave that yielded homo-floresciences remains.

00:05:27.944 --> 00:05:34.418
A Dundee-based firm secured a 2-million-pound Gates Foundation grant to advance early-stage

00:05:34.418 --> 00:05:39.898
research on pathogens affecting low- and middle-income countries, as Streamline Feed reported.

00:05:40.458 --> 00:05:44.558
The grant supports integration into the Gates Foundation's Global Health Discovery

00:05:44.558 --> 00:05:49.358
Collaboratory Network, providing access to shared assays and compound libraries.

00:05:50.405 --> 00:05:55.845
Magnesium, in an explanation from Rhonda Patrick, participates in the liver and kidney conversions

00:05:55.845 --> 00:06:01.665
that produce active calcitriol, it also aids parathyroid hormone secretion that helps regulate

00:06:01.665 --> 00:06:07.105
vitamin D balance. Nearly half of Americans fall short of estimated magnesium requirements

00:06:07.105 --> 00:06:13.509
from food and beverages. In brief, U.S. authorities launched an investigation into the Novartis gene

00:06:13.509 --> 00:06:20.089
therapy Zoolgensma. The Food and Drug Administration, or FDA, is examining possible tumor risk

00:06:20.089 --> 00:06:26.209
associated with that same Novartis gene therapy. China researchers used a chemogenetic gene therapy

00:06:26.209 --> 00:06:32.489
approach combined with clasopene that produced an average 92.6% drop in seizure frequency

00:06:32.489 --> 00:06:35.769
in three patients with drug-resistant hippocampal sclerosis.

00:06:36.609 --> 00:06:41.249
Early hearing loss gene therapy results have experts calling for longer safety follow-up.

00:06:41.809 --> 00:06:47.669
UC San Francisco researchers engineered B-Sync CAR T cells that eliminated diffuse midline

00:06:47.669 --> 00:06:52.189
glioma in two mouse models after the therapy activated only inside the brain.

00:06:52.189 --> 00:06:57.789
A Colombian fossil site shows diverse marine predators co-existing as older groups declined

00:06:57.789 --> 00:07:01.269
and newer ones appeared without a mass extinction boundary.

00:07:01.669 --> 00:07:07.329
Before we go, the FDA review of tumor risk with Zalgenzma is the safety decision now sitting

00:07:07.329 --> 00:07:08.489
with U.S. regulators.

